WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:08.163
A circle has a diameter, the distance straight across through the centre. The radius is half of that.

00:08.613 --> 00:16.814
The distance around a circle is called the circumference. It is always a little more than three times the diameter.

00:16.814 --> 00:20.594
That number is called pi, about three point one four.

00:21.044 --> 00:26.955
To find the circumference, multiply pi by the diameter. With a diameter of ten,

00:26.955 --> 00:31.145
three point one four times ten is thirty-one point four.

00:31.595 --> 00:37.985
The area is the space inside. Multiply pi by the radius, and by the radius again.

00:37.985 --> 00:43.507
With a radius of five, that is three point one four times twenty-five.

00:43.957 --> 00:49.055
Three point one four times twenty-five is seventy-eight point five.

00:49.055 --> 00:53.848
Circumference is the distance around. Area is the space inside.
